</figure>
<figure id="A1.F7" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2602.21684v1/supp_mode.png" id="A1.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:543/428;" width="543" height="428" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>
Qualitative visualization of the Primary Mode Policy (<math id="A1.F7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>) at keyframes from four different simulation tasks.
Each row corresponds to a single task episode. Within each row, three keyframes show the point cloud observation (left) and the corresponding predicted probability distribution over the discrete primary modes (right) as a heatmap. The vertical axis of the heatmap represents the mode index. The shifting patterns in the heatmaps demonstrate that the policy learns a dynamic, context-dependent mapping from observation to a belief over high-level actions as the task progresses.
</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>MeanFlow Derivation</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section provides a detailed derivation of the training objective for our mode-conditioned MeanFlow policy, as mentioned in Section 3.4. The formulation is based on the principles introduced by MeanFlow <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">Geng et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, which models the <span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">average velocity</span> of a generative path rather than the <span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">instantaneous velocity</span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let the path between a noise sample <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{0}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{0}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math> and the target action residual <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta a</annotation></semantics></math> be defined by an interpolation <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> for a time variable <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. The instantaneous velocity at time <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> is denoted by <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v(z_{r},r)=\frac{dz_{r}}{dr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v(z_{r},r)=\frac{dz_{r}}{dr}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The core concept is to define an <span id="A1.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">average velocity field</span> <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{v}(z_{r},\tau,r;o,m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{v}(z_{r},\tau,r;o,m)</annotation></semantics></math> over an arbitrary time interval <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\tau,r]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\tau,r]</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math> is the observation and <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> is the selected primary mode. This field is formally defined as the displacement between two points on the path, divided by the time interval:</p>
<table id="A1.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{v}(z_{r},\tau,r;o,m)\triangleq\frac{1}{r-\tau}\int_{\tau}^{r}v(z_{s},s;o,m)ds," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{v}(z_{r},\tau,r;o,m)\triangleq\frac{1}{r-\tau}\int_{\tau}^{r}v(z_{s},s;o,m)ds,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> is the integration variable for time. To make this definition amenable to training, we first rewrite it by clearing the denominator:</p>
<table id="A1.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(r-\tau)\bar{v}(z_{r},\tau,r;o,m)=\int_{\tau}^{r}v(z_{s},s;o,m)ds." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(r-\tau)\bar{v}(z_{r},\tau,r;o,m)=\int_{\tau}^{r}v(z_{s},s;o,m)ds.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Next, we differentiate both sides with respect to the end time <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, treating the start time <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> as a constant. Applying the product rule to the left-hand side and the Fundamental Theorem of Calculus to the right-hand side yields:</p>
<table id="A1.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{dr}\left[(r-\tau)\bar{v}(z_{r},\tau,r)\right]=\frac{d}{dr}\int_{\tau}^{r}v(z_{s},s)ds," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{dr}\left[(r-\tau)\bar{v}(z_{r},\tau,r)\right]=\frac{d}{dr}\int_{\tau}^{r}v(z_{s},s)ds,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A1.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{v}(z_{r},\tau,r)+(r-\tau)\frac{d}{dr}\bar{v}(z_{r},\tau,r)=v(z_{r},r)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{v}(z_{r},\tau,r)+(r-\tau)\frac{d}{dr}\bar{v}(z_{r},\tau,r)=v(z_{r},r).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.4" class="ltx_p">For clarity, we have omitted the conditioning on <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(o,m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(o,m)</annotation></semantics></math> in the last two steps. Rearranging the terms, we arrive at the <span id="A1.SS3.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MeanFlow Identity</span>, which establishes a fundamental relationship between the average and instantaneous velocities:</p>
<table id="A1.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{v}(z_{r},\tau,r)=v(z_{r},r)-(r-\tau)\frac{d}{dr}\bar{v}(z_{r},\tau,r)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{v}(z_{r},\tau,r)=v(z_{r},r)-(r-\tau)\frac{d}{dr}\bar{v}(z_{r},\tau,r).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.5" class="ltx_p">This identity provides a way to define a target for our neural network without computing an integral. To do so, we must first express the total time derivative <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{dr}\bar{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{dr}\bar{v}</annotation></semantics></math> in a computable form. Since <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{v}</annotation></semantics></math> is a function of <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(z_{r},\tau,r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(z_{r},\tau,r)</annotation></semantics></math>, we expand the total derivative using the chain rule:</p>
<table id="A1.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{dr}\bar{v}(z_{r},\tau,r)=\frac{\partial\bar{v}}{\partial z}\frac{dz_{r}}{dr}+\frac{\partial\bar{v}}{\partial\tau}\frac{d\tau}{dr}+\frac{\partial\bar{v}}{\partial r}\frac{dr}{dr}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{dr}\bar{v}(z_{r},\tau,r)=\frac{\partial\bar{v}}{\partial z}\frac{dz_{r}}{dr}+\frac{\partial\bar{v}}{\partial\tau}\frac{d\tau}{dr}+\frac{\partial\bar{v}}{\partial r}\frac{dr}{dr}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.6" class="ltx_p">Given that <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{dz_{r}}{dr}=v(z_{r},r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{dz_{r}}{dr}=v(z_{r},r)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d\tau}{dr}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d\tau}{dr}=0</annotation></semantics></math> (as <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>), and <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{dr}{dr}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{dr}{dr}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, the expression simplifies to:</p>
<table id="A1.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{dr}\bar{v}(z_{r},\tau,r)=v(z_{r},r)\frac{\partial\bar{v}}{\partial z}+\frac{\partial\bar{v}}{\partial r}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{dr}\bar{v}(z_{r},\tau,r)=v(z_{r},r)\frac{\partial\bar{v}}{\partial z}+\frac{\partial\bar{v}}{\partial r}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.7" class="ltx_p">Substituting this result (<a href="#A1.E13" title="In A.3 MeanFlow Derivation ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Primary-Fine Decoupling for Action Generation in Robotic Imitation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>) back into the MeanFlow Identity (<a href="#A1.E11" title="In A.3 MeanFlow Derivation ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Primary-Fine Decoupling for Action Generation in Robotic Imitation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>), we obtain an expression for the average velocity that only depends on the instantaneous velocity <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> and the partial derivatives of <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{v}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{v}(z_{r},\tau,r)=v(z_{r},r)-(r-\tau)\left(v(z_{r},r)\frac{\partial\bar{v}}{\partial z}+\frac{\partial\bar{v}}{\partial r}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{v}(z_{r},\tau,r)=v(z_{r},r)-(r-\tau)\left(v(z_{r},r)\frac{\partial\bar{v}}{\partial z}+\frac{\partial\bar{v}}{\partial r}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.8" class="ltx_p">This equation forms the basis for our training objective. We parameterize the average velocity field with a neural network <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{v}_{\theta}(z_{r},\tau,r;o,m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{v}_{\theta}(z_{r},\tau,r;o,m)</annotation></semantics></math>. The right-hand side of the equation becomes the regression target, where we replace the true partial derivatives of <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{v}</annotation></semantics></math> with those of our network <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{v}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{v}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>. Following standard practice, we apply a stop-gradient operator, <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{sg}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>sg</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{sg}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, to the target to prevent backpropagation through the Jacobian-vector products, which stabilizes training.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The resulting target, <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{v}_{tgt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{v}_{tgt}</annotation></semantics></math>, is:</p>
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{v}_{tgt}=v(z_{r},r)-(r-\tau)\left(v(z_{r},r)\frac{\partial\bar{v}_{\theta}}{\partial z}+\frac{\partial\bar{v}_{\theta}}{\partial r}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{v}_{tgt}=v(z_{r},r)-(r-\tau)\left(v(z_{r},r)\frac{\partial\bar{v}_{\theta}}{\partial z}+\frac{\partial\bar{v}_{\theta}}{\partial r}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">The instantaneous velocity <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v(z_{r},r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v(z_{r},r)</annotation></semantics></math> is substituted with the conditional velocity (i.e., the ground-truth residual <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta a</annotation></semantics></math> minus the initial noise <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>). The final loss function is the expected squared <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> error between our network’s prediction and this supervised target:</p>
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{\Delta a,z_{0},\tau,r}\left\|\bar{v}_{\theta}(z_{r},\tau,r;o,m)-\text{sg}(\bar{v}_{tgt})\right\|_{2}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext>sg</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{\Delta a,z_{0},\tau,r}\left\|\bar{v}_{\theta}(z_{r},\tau,r;o,m)-\text{sg}(\bar{v}_{tgt})\right\|_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.3" class="ltx_p">This objective allows the network <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{v}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{v}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> to learn the average velocity field directly, enabling efficient one-step generation of the action residual <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta a</annotation></semantics></math> at inference time.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Implementation and Training Hyperparameters</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This subsection details the key hyperparameters used for training and implementing our PF-DAG.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T6" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A1.T6.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A1.T6.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T6.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A1.T6.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hyperparameter</span></th>
<th id="A1.T6.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A1.T6.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Description</span></th>
<th id="A1.T6.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A1.T6.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Value</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A1.T6.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T6.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Prediction Horizon <math id="A1.T6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T6.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">The total number of timesteps in a predicted action chunk.</td>
<td id="A1.T6.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">32 / 16</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T6.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T6.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Execution Horizon <math id="A1.T6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{a}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T6.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">The number of timesteps from the chunk executed before re-planning.</td>
<td id="A1.T6.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center">16 / 8</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T6.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T6.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Learning Rate</td>
<td id="A1.T6.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">The peak learning rate after the warmup phase.</td>
<td id="A1.T6.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center">1e-4</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T6.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T6.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Weight Decay</td>
<td id="A1.T6.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">The weight decay value for the AdamW optimizer.</td>
<td id="A1.T6.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center">0.01</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T6.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T6.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Batch Size</td>
<td id="A1.T6.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">The number of samples processed per training step.</td>
<td id="A1.T6.2.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center">128</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T6.2.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T6.2.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Codebook Size <math id="A1.T6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T6.2.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">The number of discrete primary modes in the VQ-VAE codebook.</td>
<td id="A1.T6.2.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center">64</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T6.2.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T6.2.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Commitment Weight <math id="A1.T6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T6.2.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">The weight of the commitment loss term in the VQ-VAE objective.</td>
<td id="A1.T6.2.8.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center">0.25</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T6.2.9" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T6.2.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">VQ-VAE Latent Dim</td>
<td id="A1.T6.2.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">The dimensionality of the VQ-VAE latent space.</td>
<td id="A1.T6.2.9.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">64</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span>Hyperparameters for the PF-DAG framework.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>Ablation Study on Mode Number</h3>

<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We present more results on mode number <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, as seen in Table <a href="#A1.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ A.5 Ablation Study on Mode Number ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Primary-Fine Decoupling for Action Generation in Robotic Imitation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T7" class="ltx_table">
<div id="A1.T7.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:278.2pt;height:77.5pt;vertical-align:-36.8pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-35.4pt,9.9pt) scale(0.797243060322402,0.797243060322402) ;">
<table id="A1.T7.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A1.T7.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T7.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt">Ablations</th>
<th id="A1.T7.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" colspan="3">Benchmarks</th>
<th id="A1.T7.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"></th></tr>
<tr id="A1.T7.2.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T7.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r"># Modes</th>
<th id="A1.T7.2.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column">Adroit (3)</th>
<th id="A1.T7.2.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column">DexArt (4)</th>
<th id="A1.T7.2.1.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r">MetaWorld (11)</th>
<th id="A1.T7.2.1.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column">Weighted Success</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A1.T7.2.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T7.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">64</td>
<td id="A1.T7.2.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A1.T7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.77\scriptstyle{\pm 0.03}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.77</mn><mo mathsize="0.700em">±</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">0.03</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.77\scriptstyle{\pm 0.03}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
